{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1539783-defense-questions","id":1539783,"title":"Defense questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-04T00:17:24-07:00","id":1539783,"title":"Defense questions","content":"As an action you can roll stamina to buy defense tricks. But you can also take an action to go full defense, rolling twice your stamina to buy defense tricks. If they both take an action, why would you ever go for normal defense? And since characters only get one action per turn, does that mean if you take a defense action you can't act on your turn, or if you've already had your turn you can't use a defense action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:30:28-07:00","id":1539905,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, a defensive action where you are rolling Stamina alone is a reflexive action. The write up doesn't say its reflexive, but you always take them in response to someone else's attack outside of your turn. Later on, it also says a character can &quot;give up her action to reset her Defense by rolling again.&quot; Implying that the first Defense roll never takes up your action.<br /> <br /> <br /> Full defense, on the other hand, takes up your regular action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T22:43:43-07:00","id":1539977,"title":"","content":"So, if a character uses a reflexive action to roll a regular defense, then later in the round wants to spend an action to defend themselves better, can they use that action to make a full defence roll instead? Or is it that once you set your defense the only thing you can do is spend an action to reroll the same defense? So a character that uses a reflexive action to defend is stuck with that for the rest of the round?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 08-07-2024, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T11:53:20-07:00","id":1540093,"title":"","content":"Full Defense is specifically called out as a Simple Action. Under the Action Sequence header, Reflexive and Simple Actions are listed as distinct things. Which leads me to believe that you cannot take Full Defense reflexively - it has to happen on your initiative. The other rolls are still reflexive and can happen at any time.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong, but that is the implication I have from reading the rules so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}